<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.somm.totalwine</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/danielguerrero/dev/wine_app/backend/scripts/run_totalwine_launchd.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/danielguerrero/dev/wine_app/backend</string>

    <!-- WEEKLY, Sunday 06:30 CT. Was StartInterval 864000 ("every 10 days"),
         which NEVER FIRED ONCE: StartInterval counts from when the job is
         LOADED, so the 2026-08-28 reboot restarted the clock, and `launchctl
         print` showed `runs = 0` on 2026-09-06. A schedule that silently resets
         is not a schedule. StartCalendarInterval is wall-clock, so a reboot
         cannot postpone it and launchd runs a missed occurrence at the next
         opportunity.

         Weekly, not 10-daily, for two reasons. The staleness bench is 10 days,
         so a 10-day probe sits exactly ON it — even a working probe left Total
         Wine at the edge of invisible (the runner script flagged this itself).
         And 10 days of near-total quiet demonstrably did NOT clear the block:
         probed 2026-09-06 after the canary had never run, still HTTP 403
         (PerimeterX). So the "PX decays with quiet" reasoning behind the
         original cadence is weakened, and spacing probes further apart buys
         nothing.

         The cost of a blocked week is still exactly one request — is_blocked()
         makes a single GET and the runner stops there — so weekly probing does
         not resemble the hundreds of rapid pageSize=200 fetches that earned the
         block. Runs after H-E-B (05:30) to avoid overlapping it.

         Every result appends to ~/Library/Logs/somm-totalwine-probes.tsv so the
         decay curve is measured rather than assumed. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>6</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/danielguerrero/Library/Logs/somm-totalwine.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/danielguerrero/Library/Logs/somm-totalwine.err.log</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
